    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/security-specialist-i-campus-locksmith": {
      "title": "Security Specialist I (Campus Locksmith) -",
      "description": "Security Specialist I (Campus Locksmith) - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Security Specialist I (Campus Locksmith) Public Safety Staff, full-time (32+ hours per week) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Security Specialist I (Campus Locksmith) Position Number: 999915 Unit/Department: Public Safety Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Job Summary: The Security Specialist I (Campus Locksmith) plays a critical role in maintaining the safety, security, and accessibility of university facilities. This position is responsible for installing, maintaining, repairing, and rekeying locks, door hardware, key systems, and electronic access control devices across campus buildings. The Security Specialist is also responsible for basic fire alarm system maintenance as well as video surveillance equipment. The Security Specialist supports students, faculty, staff, and visitors by ensuring secure access to classrooms, residence halls, offices, laboratories, and other university facilities. The Security Specialist I (Campus Locksmith) is responsible for maintaining the integrity, reliability, and security of the institution’s physical access systems. This position performs skilled locksmith work with a primary focus on lock repair and key cutting (60% of duties), while also supporting electronic access control systems, security infrastructure installation, fire safety systems, and emergency response functions. This role carries a high level of responsibility for safeguarding the campus security system, ensuring proper access control, key accountability, and rapid response to security-related incidents. The position requires participation in after-hours and on-call response for all assigned functional areas. Minimum Qualifications: * High school diploma or equivalent * Experience in locksmithing, facilities maintenance, or related trade *Familiarity with fire safety systems. *Knowledge of mechanical locking systems and key cutting * Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive security information * Valid driver’s license Preferred Qualifications: * Experience with fire safety systems * Experience with installing and maintaining video systems Job Duties: 60% - Lock Repair & Key Cutting - (Essential) 15% - Electronic Lock & Access Control Systems - (Essential) 10% - Fire Safety & Life Safety Systems - (Essential) 5% - Camera Installation & Wiring - (Essential) 5% - Emergency Elevator Response - (Essential) % - Other Duties as Assigned - (Essential) Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online.  Please include a resume and cover letter. Review of Applications Begins: A review of applications will begin immediately.  This position will remain open until filled. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email Scott.law@drake.edu Salary and Benefits: At Drake, we are proud to offer our employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents a comprehensive benefits package, which includes a wide range of core benefits, perks, and discounts. If you are exploring a job with Drake University, we invite you to spend a little time with our Drake Benefits Guide 2026 . One of our popular policies provides a tuition waiver for Drake employees, their spouses, and eligible dependents. Drake also participates in not one, but two tuition exchange programs available to dependent children. Tuition Benefits For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 2f98446e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Public Safety Public Safety First Name (required) 989b5560 Last Name (required) 8d243e87 Email (required) 1477fd54 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 569f8455 Last Name (required) 68e9f148 Email (required) 50e7fce7 Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with d6bf91a1 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) c63a0b72 Last Name (required) 4b3c5b90 Email (required) 858feaab Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO About Drake Academics Admission Campus Life Online Athletics Alumni News & Events Giving College of Arts & Sciences Zimpleman College of Business John Dee Bright College School of Education School of Journalism & Mass Communication Law School College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Cowles Library Employment Giving to Drake COVID-19: Our Response Information Technology Services Consumer Information Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Privacy Statement Do Not Sell My Information © 2022 Drake University. All rights reserved. Candidate Details Please choose the department(s)"
