    "https://jobs.drake.edu/jobs/sports-media-and-communication-graduate-assistant-ssmcga": {
      "title": "Sports Media and Communication Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Sports Media and Communication Graduate Assistant - SSMCGA - Home (current) About Drake Mission & Values Working at Drake Benefits Overview Living in Des Moines Contact Us Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Sports Media and Communication Graduate Assistant - SSMCGA Journalism Multimedia Staff, part-time without benefits (less than 20 hours per week) Add to favorites View favorites Title: Sports Media and Communication Graduate Assistant - SSMCGA Position Number: SSMCGA Unit/Department: Journalism Multimedia Salary: Hourly rate Department Summary: Drake University is a forward-thinking community of scholars with a focus on active, collaborative learning and applied scholarship. Drake is in Des Moines, Iowa—a vibrant city that is nationally recognized for its quality of life and a wealth of opportunities for professional, social and civic engagement. A Drake education couples hands-on training in professional skills with a strong liberal arts education. We strive to create a community of scholars that represents the complexity of the human experience in regards to race, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, economic status, gender identification, religion, age and physical abilities. We are committed to creating a welcoming and supportive environment for all our faculty, staff, students and visitors. We develop and offer innovative programming serving a variety of audiences, including high school, undergraduate, and graduate students, as well as community members, industry professionals, and retirees. The successful applicant will join a collegial, welcoming, energetic and supportive community. Job Summary: The Sports Media and Communication Graduate Assistant serves as a liaison between the School of Journalism and Mass Communication and the University’s NCAA Division I Athletics Department. This position is designed to provide professional experience for a graduate student while also supporting student success, experiential learning opportunities, and collaborative initiatives that connect academic programs with Drake Athletics. The Graduate Assistant will help cultivate meaningful partnerships that enhance student learning, career preparation, and engagement in sports media, strategic communication, sports journalism, sports broadcasting, and digital content creation. Responsibilities will include: Student Engagement and Academic Support • Identify and coordinate opportunities for student involvement in athletics-related communication, media production, content creation, marketing, broadcasting, and public relations activities. • Serve as a mentor and resource for undergraduate students pursuing sports media and communication careers. • Assist students in identifying experiential learning opportunities within Drake Athletics. • Support recruitment, retention, and engagement efforts for sports media and communication majors. • Facilitate networking opportunities between students, alumni, Athletics personnel, and industry professionals. • Coordinate workshops, panels, and professional development events focused on careers in sports media and communication. • Support communication and project coordination between SJMC faculty and staff, Athletics staff, and students. Outreach and Assessment • Promote sports media and communication opportunities through digital communication channels and outreach efforts. • Help maintain relationships with alumni and industry partners working in sports media and communication fields. • Track student participation and outcomes associated with athletics-based experiential learning opportunities. • Collect and analyze data related to student engagement, experiential learning participation, and partnership effectiveness, and assist with the creation of reports, presentations, and promotional materials highlighting partnership outcomes and student achievements. Through this assistantship, the Graduate Assistant will: • Develop leadership and student mentorship skills. • Gain experience building and managing cross-campus partnerships. • Strengthen strategic communication and project management competencies. • Expand professional expertise in sports media and collegiate athletics. • Build a portfolio of applied work connecting academic programs with a Division I athletics program. The Graduate Assistant reports to the dean of the Drake School of Journalism and Mass Communication and works closely with designated Athletics Department personnel. Regular collaboration with faculty, staff, coaches, and student leaders is expected. Compensation This is an hourly position restricted to no more than 20 hours per week while school is in session. Tuition in one of Drake's graduate programs will be provided in accordance with university graduate assistantship policies. To remain eligible, the Graduate Assistant must remain enrolled in at least 9 credits each semester in a Drake University graduate program and remain in good academic standing. Minimum Qualifications: • Admission to and enrollment in a Drake University graduate degree program. • Bachelor’s degree in journalism, communication, public relations, strategic communication, sports management, media production, or a related field. • Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. • Demonstrated organizational and project management abilities. • Interest in sports media, athletics communications, athletics productions, and student development. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience working in collegiate athletics, sports media, journalism, broadcasting, strategic communication, marketing, or public relations. • Experience mentoring or advising undergraduate students. • Familiarity with NCAA athletics and collegiate sports communication environments. • Experience with social media, digital content creation, video production, or event coordination. Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, you must apply online. Please include a resume and cover letter. If you have any questions about this job positing or the application process, please email kelly.bruhn@drake.edu Review of Applications Begins: A review of applications will begin immediately. This position will remain open until filled. For faculty positions, selection will depend on the receipt of recommendation confirming the candidate's scholarly achievements and teaching abilities and/or on the candidate's satisfactory passing of a teaching demonstration if selected for an on-campus interview. For staff positions, selection will depend upon careful review of each applicant’s references, education, and, if applicable, experience. ABOUT DRAKE Drake University is recognized as a top private university in the Midwest. Drake is a midsize university in Des Moines, Iowa, with an increasingly diverse student body. We are deeply committed to equity and inclusion and creating a sense of belonging for all members of the campus community—faculty, staff, and students alike. More than 900 faculty and staff are part of the Bulldog pack, a close-knit group of colleagues enthusiastic about preparing students to be global citizens and leaders, challenging assumptions. Drake University is not only an outstanding institution of higher learning, it is also a wonderful place to work. We are enthusiastically committed to welcoming new ideas and people into the fold, and to retaining and rewarding stellar employees. All positions at Drake provide opportunities to contribute to Drake University’s core mission of creating an exceptional learning environment that prepares students of all backgrounds for meaningful lives and professional accomplishments. STRONG COMMITMENT TO A DIVERSE AND INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY At Drake University, we don’t just accept differences—we celebrate them, we support them, and we thrive on them for the benefit of our students, our employees, and our community. As reflected in our Core Values, we embrace a diverse and inclusive community. EQUAL OPPORTUNITY Drake University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. We provide equal employment opportunities to all individuals regardless of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.  Drake University is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodations in its services, programs, activities, education, and employment for individuals with disabilities. If you would benefit from an accommodation at any point in the recruitment process (including using our online application process), please contact Drake Human Resources (p: 515.271.3133; e: jobs@drake.edu ) and let us know how we can assist you. Apply Now Sign up for Job Alerts! Job Alert 324b9714 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Journalism Multimedia Journalism Multimedia First Name (required) 479378bf Last Name (required) 6971e242 Email (required) 7d2e0884 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) d4a6bc09 Last Name (required) bf8ec8a1 Email (required) 9fae61d3 Please enter the information of the person you would like to share this job with fb770b33 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply for position First Name (required) ef61c26b Last Name (required) 5ba3acea Email (required) 11d75477 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you 2507 University Ave.   Des Moines, IA 50311 515-271-2011 Maps & Directions University Calendar Contact Directory Public Safety VISIT APPLY REQUEST INFO About Drake Academics Admission Campus Life Online Athletics Alumni News & Events Giving College of Arts & Sciences Zimpleman College of Business John Dee Bright College School of Education School of Journalism & Mass Communication Law School College of Pharmacy & Health Sciences Cowles Library Employment Giving to Drake COVID-19: Our Response Information Technology Services Consumer Information Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Nondiscrimination & Accessibility Privacy Statement Do Not Sell My Information © 2022 Drake University. All rights reserved. Candidate Details Please choose the department(s)"
